WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.207
Hi, I'm Mallow!

00:00:02.207 --> 00:00:06.179
Kev turns a Qwen3.5 base into a model that picks from a list.

00:00:06.179 --> 00:00:08.623
Here's how it points, and what that costs.

00:00:10.183 --> 00:00:13.708
Every option is a span in one shared sequence, and a small

00:00:13.708 --> 00:00:14.883
head points at one.

00:00:14.883 --> 00:00:17.821
The options can see each other, so their order matters.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:22.360
The question and every option go into one sequence.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.538
Each option ends in a closing tag, and a decide token comes last.

00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:30.299
Qwen3.5 with a rank-sixteen LoRA reads it all.

00:00:30.299 --> 00:00:34.476
Its vocabulary head is dropped, because nothing is ever generated.

00:00:34.896 --> 00:00:38.786
A small head projects each option's end state and the decide state

00:00:38.786 --> 00:00:42.352
to two hundred and fifty-six numbers, and takes a dot product:

00:00:42.352 --> 00:00:43.648
one score per option.

00:00:44.068 --> 00:00:47.220
Send two options or sixteen, and no weight changes shape.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.111
The option set is just data.

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:53.668
The repository measured this two hundred and fifty-nine times.

00:00:53.668 --> 00:00:58.389
Shuffle the options, and fifteen point three percent of answers flip on the prototype.

00:00:58.389 --> 00:01:01.086
On a nine B base, one point eight.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:05.487
The fix exists: give every option its own branch.

00:01:05.487 --> 00:01:09.380
Then nothing flips, but it cost five point eight points at four

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:12.624
B, and on Qwen3.5 the recurrent layers can't do it.

00:01:13.044 --> 00:01:16.872
So Kev ships the shared context, and the flips shrink with scale instead.

00:01:18.558 --> 00:01:21.304
Order sensitivity is a dial, not a switch.

00:01:21.304 --> 00:01:23.363
And the dial is mostly capacity.

00:01:25.608 --> 00:01:29.443
To recap: options share one sequence, a small head points at one,

00:01:29.443 --> 00:01:31.041
and scale shrinks the flips.

00:01:31.461 --> 00:01:33.452
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:33.452 --> 00:01:34.021
I'm Mallow.

00:01:34.021 --> 00:01:34.306
Bye!
